# MUST Computing Onboarding Sandbox 🎯

Welcome to the sandbox! This repository exists for one reason: **to give you a safe space to practice Git and GitHub workflows without the fear of breaking anything.**

If you have never opened a Pull Request (PR) before, this is exactly where you start.

---

## 🛠️ The Challenge: Leave Your Mark

Your mission is to add your profile to our community roster file.

### Step 1: Request Invitation
Before you can push or open a PR inside the organization, ensure you are an official member. If you haven't been added yet, contact an admin or open an issue in this repository with your GitHub username.

### Step 2: Set Up Locally
Clone this repository to your development machine:

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/mucosamust/onboarding.git](https://github.com/your-org-name/onboarding.git)
cd onboarding
```

### Step 3: Create a Branch

Following our ```CONTRIBUTING.md``` guidelines, create a feature branch using your username:

```bash
git checkout -b feat/add-profile-yourusername
```

### Step 4: Add Your Details
Open the file named ```ROSTER.md``` in your favorite editor (e.g., Neovim, VS Code).

Append a new row to the table with your details. Use the format below:

| Your Name | Tech Track / Interests | Favorite Tool/Editor |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Jane Doe | Android Dev (Compose), Distributed Systems | Neovim |

### Step 5: Commit and Push

Stage your changes, commit using a descriptive message, and push your branch:

```bash
git add ROSTER.md
git commit -m "feat(roster): add [Your Name] to community roster"
git push origin feat/add-profile-yourusername
```

### Step 6: Open the PR

Go to the main repository page on GitHub, click Compare & pull request, fill out a quick description, and submit. A peer or maintainer will review and merge it!

## ⚠️ What if I encounter a Merge Conflict?

If someone else edits ```ROSTER.md``` at the same time, GitHub might tell you that your branch has conflicts. Don't panic! This is a core part of learning Git:

1. Pull the latest changes from main: ```git pull origin main```

2. Open ```ROSTER.md```, look for the conflict markers (<<<<<<<, =======, >>>>>>>), choose how to combine the entries, and delete the markers.

3. Commit the fix and push again.

*You're officially on your way to becoming an open-source contributor! 🚀*